    "collected_at": "2026-11-23T10:26:06.921743+00:00",
    "origin_id": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/chinese-air-taxi-completes-sri-lankas-first-passenger-carrying-autonomous-evtol-flight-278835.html",
    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/chinese-air-taxi-completes-sri-lankas-first-passenger-carrying-autonomous-evtol-flight-278835.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-11-23T10:05:49+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-11-23T10:05:49+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-11-23T10:27:18.194683+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-23T10:27:18.194683+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • MTPeak Stole Some of the Spotlight at EICMA 2026 With Insane Power and Retro Looks on Three Wheels\nChinese Air Taxi Completes Sri Lanka’s First Passenger-Carrying Autonomous eVTOL Flight\n7 photos\nPhoto: EHang\nEHang adds another international industry-first under its belt, as one of its pilotless aircraft carries out the first-ever passenger-carrying autonomous eVTOL (electric vertical takeoff and landing) flight in Sri Lanka.\nThe passengers of this historic flight with no pilot onboard were Sri Lankan officials, Minister Karunathilaka and Deputy Minister Kodithuwakku. The EH216-S aircraft carried out this inaugural flight in Colombo, as part of a wider ceremony attended by numerous Sri Lankan and Chinese officials.\nWith this flight, Sri Lanka officially becomes the 24th country where the EHang EH216-S has completed flight demonstrations. For the Chinese company, it marks another significant milestone, as its first official flight in South Asia. Sri Lanka is a special partner for EHang, as the first country that has adopted the EHang Global Fast Track Program back in August 2026.\nThrough this program, the Chinese eVTOL maker actively works with national and local players in the private sector and authorities to establish an AAM (Advanced Air Mobility) ecosystem, including the regulatory framework, vertiports, air taxi routes, and other essential pillars for autonomous eVTOL operations.\nIn Sri Lanka, as well as the other countries who are part of the program, the EH216-S won’t be limited to air taxi service. While primarily geared toward aerial tourism, this pilotless electric aircraft can also be used in search-and-rescue missions, disaster relief, and critical logistics for hard-to-reach areas that are typically more isolated.\nThe EH216 has completed more than 100,000 safe flights to this date, with no pilot onboard. A newly-established strategic hub in Thailand will focus on EHang’s expansion in Southeast Asia, while Kazakhstan is at the center of its Central Asia strategy. Last year, the Chinese company confirmed plans to launch large-scale production in Kazakhstan, following a collaboration with Allur Group, a big automotive manufacturing company in the area.\nThe collaboration targets what could become the first-ever eVTOL assembly facility in Central Asia, with a production capacity of around 200 aircraft per year.\nIn 2025, EHang has also completed the first passenger-carrying autonomous eVTOL flight in Africa. It took place in Kigali, Rwanda, during the 9th Aviation Africa Summit and Exhibition, with support from China Road and Bridge Corporation (CRBC).\nNone of these pioneering flight demonstrations with passengers onboard would have been possible without one thing: the EH216-S was the first passenger autonomous eVTOL in the world to secure full certification. China's civil aviation authority was much faster than its international counterparts in establishing all the certification requirements and regulations, allowing EHang to also move much faster through the whole process.\nThe Chinese eVTOL maker now has all the certifications in hand to focus on global expansion, including the PC (Production Certificate) that allows it to mass-produce autonomous aircraft in the EH216 series (passenger and cargo).\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nChinese eVTOL Chinese autonomous eVTOL Ehang EH216-S eVTOL evtol air taxi\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Otilia Drăgan\nOtilia believes that if it’s eco, green, or groundbreaking, people should know about it (especially if it's got wheels or wings). Working in online media for over five years, she's gained a deeper perspective on how people everywhere can inspire each other. Full profile\nUP NEXT Pontiac Firebird Trans Am Spent Over 40 Years Abandoned in a Closed Dealership, Now It's Finally Out",
